To terminate a C program, you can use the `exit()` function from the `stdlib.h` library. This function causes the program to terminate and returns a status code to the operating system.

Here is a basic example of how to use `exit()`:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    exit(0);  // Terminate the program with status code 0
    // The code below this line will not be executed
    printf("This line will not be printed.\n");
